igos-openssl-fips-provider (3.1.2-1igos2) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Conflicts/Replaces/Provides openssl-provider-fips: Debian's OpenSSL 3.5
    builds an unvalidated 3.5 fips.so at the same ossl-modules/fips.so path.
  * Ship fips.so byte-for-byte as built (disable dh_strip/dh_dwz, which were
    stripping the validated module and adding .gnu_debuglink).
  * Self-test the staged module at build time and refuse to package it unless
    it reports the pinned provider version.
  * Ship an identity manifest (version + SHA-256) that vyos-1x verifies before
    and after activating FIPS mode.

